1	# GraphRAG Benchmark Demo
2	
3	Companion code for the "Benchmarking RAG for Accuracy" webinar. A small
4	GraphRAG pipeline (LangChain4j + Neo4j) over a made-up software-support
5	knowledge graph, plus a benchmark harness that scores it across question
6	types with an LLM-as-judge.
7	
8	## What's here
9	
10	```
11	src/main/java/com/neo4j/webinar/
12	  Config.java                        env-var driven config (Neo4j + OpenAI)
13	  SupportAssistant.java               the LangChain4j AiServices interface
14	  Main.java                           entry point: seed, sanity-check, benchmark
15	  ingest/GraphSeeder.java             loads the demo graph + embeds chunks
16	  retrieval/GraphRagContentRetriever.java   vector seed + 1-hop graph expansion
17	  retrieval/VectorOnlyContentRetriever.java bonus: vector-only baseline for comparison
18	  bench/BenchmarkQuestion.java        one row of the benchmark
19	  bench/ScoredAnswer.java             one graded result
20	  bench/LlmJudgeScorer.java           LLM-as-judge grading
21	  bench/BenchmarkRunner.java          runs + reports + writes CSV
22	src/main/resources/benchmark_questions.json   the 12-question benchmark set
23	```
24	
25	The demo domain: two fictional products (Aurora, Beacon), their releases,
26	bugs, features, customers, and support tickets, plus two policy documents.
27	Small enough to hold in your head during the talk, connected enough to need
28	graph traversal for the interesting questions.
